## SQ-SB-01 | spawn boxes load
@group B
@commands boot; `grep -E '\[spawn-boxes\]\|\[spawner-filter\]' logs/latest.log`
@pass `17 box(es)` (15 until the end_tower and allay_temples boxes, 2026-11-06); after the first spawns `N structure(s) boxed` (about 75), no `is in box` warning, no `no pool` / `no entity type` (ST-321)
@fails 0 boxes: `spawn_boxes.json` missing or unreadable (error line)
@from batches/r1031/w2_metas_spawns.qb
# r1118 R1 (2026-11-18): 17 is intended: spawn_boxes.json gained end_tower (mobs/pillagers #2) and allay_temples (mobs/spawns #5)
bootexpect \[spawn-boxes\].*17 box\(es\)
bootreject \[spawn-boxes\].*(no pool|no entity type|is in box)
> pbot spawn qa 0 120 0 minecraft:overworld creative
> gamerule doDaylightCycle false
> time set 18000
look after the first spawns the log has "N structure(s) boxed" (about 75); re-check at the end of the batch

## SQ-SB-02 | no pillager spawners in the templates
@group B
@commands `/cdevplace` `illager_siege_weapons:catapult`, `mysticrift_pillagers_towers_aris:oak_wood_pillager_tower`, `blocky_siege:pillager_ship`, `mysticrift_pillagers_towers_aris:end_pillager_tower` (in the End)
@pass no spawner block in any; a `[spawner-filter] ... removed` line per template, the End tower's with `plus 2 with no mob` (ST-320)
@fails spawner left: its NBT shape (not `SpawnData.entity.id`), `TemplateSpawnerFilter.entities`
@from batches/r1031/w2_metas_spawns.qb
> execute positioned 3000 100 3000 run ceplace structures illager_siege_weapons:catapult mysticrift_pillagers_towers_aris:oak_wood_pillager_tower blocky_siege:pillager_ship
> execute in minecraft:the_end run ceplace structures mysticrift_pillagers_towers_aris:end_pillager_tower
waitlog \[ceplace\] done 600
reject \[ceplace\] done.* [1-9]\d* failed
expect \[spawner-filter\].*removed
expect \[spawner-filter\].*plus 2 with no mob
look no spawner block in any (cdevtest count around the logged placements for minecraft:spawner: n=0); /ceplace syntax per memory worldgen-config-ceplace if the command is rejected

## SQ-SB-03 | lone large pillager tower: illager mix at night, pillagers only by day
@group B
@commands `/locate structure mysticrift_pillagers_towers_aris:birch_pillager_tower` (a lone one, not in a meta); wait 3-5 min at night, then `/time set day` 3 min; `/kill @e[type=!player,distance=..64]` between
@pass night: pillagers, vindicators, evokers, illusioners, witches, no ravager, no zombie or creeper inside; day: only pillagers (ST-322)
@fails biome mobs inside: mixin not applied (boot log mixin error) or tag `meta/pillager_large_towers` empty
@from batches/r1031/w2_metas_spawns.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> locate structure mysticrift_pillagers_towers_aris:birch_pillager_tower
waitlog nearest mysticrift_pillagers_towers_aris:birch_pillager_tower is at|type "?mysticrift_pillagers_towers_aris:birch_pillager_tower|mysticrift_pillagers_towers_aris:birch_pillager_tower.*timed out 330
capture BT is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> tp qa {BT1+30} 100 {BT3}
> time set 18000
sleep 20
> cdevtest tickwarp 4400
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=4400 asked=4400 300
> execute positioned {BT1} 80 {BT3} if entity @e[type=minecraft:pillager,distance=..48]
> execute positioned {BT1} 80 {BT3} if entity @e[type=minecraft:vindicator,distance=..48]
> execute positioned {BT1} 80 {BT3} if entity @e[type=minecraft:evoker,distance=..48]
> execute positioned {BT1} 80 {BT3} if entity @e[type=minecraft:illusioner,distance=..48]
> execute positioned {BT1} 80 {BT3} if entity @e[type=minecraft:witch,distance=..48]
> execute positioned {BT1} 80 {BT3} if entity @e[type=minecraft:ravager,distance=..48]
> execute positioned {BT1} 80 {BT3} if entity @e[type=minecraft:zombie,distance=..48]
> execute positioned {BT1} 80 {BT3} if entity @e[type=minecraft:creeper,distance=..48]
> execute positioned {BT1} 80 {BT3} run kill @e[type=!minecraft:player,distance=..64]
> time set 6000
sleep 20
> cdevtest tickwarp 3601
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=3601 asked=3601 300
> execute positioned {BT1} 80 {BT3} if entity @e[type=minecraft:pillager,distance=..48]
> execute positioned {BT1} 80 {BT3} if entity @e[type=minecraft:vindicator,distance=..48]
> execute positioned {BT1} 80 {BT3} if entity @e[type=minecraft:witch,distance=..48]
look night: pillager, vindicator, evoker, illusioner, witch present (counts), ravager / zombie / creeper "Test failed"; day: only pillagers (ST-322). y 80 is a guess: if every check fails, read the tower's y from the locate line or a meta log line and rerun with that y
> time set 18000
reject \[cdevtest\] verb=\S+ .*error=

